<title>CANADA: First Calgary in Nigeria oil deal.</title>
<headline>First Calgary in Nigeria oil deal.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Calgary Petroleums Ltd said on Thursday it agreed with Abacan Resource Corp to participate in Nigerian oil concession block 233 in the Niger Delta.</p>
<p>Under the deal, First Calgary would obtain the right to earn 40 percent of Abacan's interest in the block after paying Abacan US$4 million.</p>
<p>Of the total, First Calgary would pay Abacan US$2 million on confirmation of Nigerian government approval and the remainder by payment of 53 percent of costs of exploration and development carried out by Abacan on the block.  </p>
<p>First Calgary said completion of the farmout arrangement was still subject to board approval.</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
